---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Uinta Watch handles your data — what the iOS app collects, why it collects it, and the choices you have. No accounts, no ads, no trackers."
>
  <a href="#main-content" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-accent focus:text-ink rounded">Skip to content</a>
  <main id="main-content">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="section-loose bg-paper border-b border-paper-3">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-6">Privacy Policy</p>
          <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink mb-8">
            Your Data,<br/>
            <span class="text-accent">On Your Terms</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-xl leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Uinta Watch collects the bare minimum — only what you choose to submit —
            and uses it solely to support early wildfire detection.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Effective date: August 30, 2026</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Policy -->
    <section class="section bg-paper">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-8">

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">1. Information the App Collects</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>
                  The App collects the following information, only when <strong>you</strong> choose to provide it:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
                  <li>
                    <strong>Location.</strong> When you use the <strong>Report</strong> feature, the App requests your device's
                    precise location (with your permission) so your fire or smoke report can be associated with the place you
                    observed it. Location is accessed only when you actively submit a report. The sensor map does not track or
                    store your location.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <strong>Photos.</strong> If you attach a photo to a report, the image you choose is included with your
                    submission. The App never accesses your photo library except when you explicitly pick an image.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <strong>Report content.</strong> The text description you type when submitting a report.
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  The App does <strong>not</strong> collect your name, email address, device identifiers, advertising
                  identifiers, or any other personal information. It has <strong>no account system, no in-app purchases, no
                  advertising, and no third-party analytics</strong>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">2. How the Information Is Used</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>Information you submit is used solely to:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
                  <li>
                    Display your report (location, description, and optional photo) to support the early warning system for
                    wildfire detection;
                  </li>
                  <li>Improve and operate the App's services.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">3. Sharing of Information</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>
                  We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or share your information with third parties for advertising,
                  marketing, or tracking purposes. Submitted reports may be visible to other users of the service and to
                  authorized emergency-response partners as part of the early warning system's purpose.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">4. Data Retention</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>
                  Report submissions are retained indefinitely to support ongoing wildfire research and the long-term
                  operation of the early warning system. Reports may be reviewed for patterns over time to improve detection
                  and to better understand fire risk in the Uinta Basin.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">5. Your Choices</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>You can control App permissions at any time through your device settings:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
                  <li>
                    <strong>Location, Camera, and Photo Library</strong> permissions can be granted or revoked in
                    <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, or per-app under <strong>Settings → Uinta Watch</strong>.
                  </li>
                  <li>You may stop using the App and delete it at any time.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">6. Children's Privacy</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>
                  The App is a general-audience utility and does not knowingly collect information from children under 13.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
              <div class="prose text-ink-soft space-y-4">
                <p>
                  We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be available at this URL, with
                  the effective date shown above.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <!-- Sidebar -->
          <div class="lg:col-span-3 lg:col-start-10">
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-4">The Short Version</h3>
              <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">
                <p>No accounts. No ads. No analytics.</p>
                <p>We only see what you submit through the Report feature — and only because you chose to share it.</p>
                <p>Your location is used just for the report, never tracked on the sensor map.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <section class="section-tight bg-paper-2 border-t border-paper-3">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-4">8. Contact</h2>
          <p class="prose text-ink-soft mb-4">
            For questions about this policy or the App, contact:
          </p>
          <div class="card inline-block">
            <p class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Uinta Watch</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mb-1">
              Email: <a href="mailto:hello@uintawatch.com" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-dark underline">hello@uintawatch.com</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
